  "nl_text": "The schemabench_0225 database is a comprehensive system for managing a training center. It includes tables for employees, clients, courses, and course materials. The trainer table contains information about the trainers, including their contact information, employment history, and qualifications. The client table contains information about the clients, including their contact information and initial enrollment date. The course table contains information about the courses, including the course length, fee, level, and course materials. The course_book table contains information about the course materials, including the book title, publisher, and list price. The author table contains information about the authors of the course materials. The course_prerequisites table contains information about the prerequisites for each course. The course_software table contains information about the software required for each course. The class table contains information about the classes, including the start and end dates, trainer, classroom, and course. The enrollment_request table contains information about the enrollment requests, including the request date, status, payment, and client. The vendor table contains information about the vendors, including their contact information. The order table contains information about the orders, including the order date, order status, and vendor. The shipment table contains information about the shipments, including the shipment date, vendor, and course materials. The order_line table contains information about the order line items, including the course book ISBN, quantity ordered, and price charged. The shipment_line table contains information about the shipment line items, including the course book ISBN and quantity received. The course_book_vendor table contains information about the course materials and their vendors.",
  "gold_question": "1. Background / Context\n   Northern Lights Technical (NLT) School, established in 1985 in Pittsfield, MA, is a leading computer software training provider in the region. Due to substantial growth, NLT's reliance on MS Excel for record-keeping has led to bookkeeping inefficiencies. A new database system is proposed to streamline operations and manage data more effectively.\n\n2. Objectives\n   Develop a comprehensive database system to replace Excel spreadsheets for improved management of trainer qualifications, course offerings, client enrollments, and book orders. The system aims to enhance data integrity, optimize scheduling, and facilitate efficient tracking of resources and client memberships.\n\n3. Stakeholders & Users\n   - Stakeholders: NLT management, trainers, administrative staff, and clients.\n   - Users: Trainers, administrative personnel, clients, and IT support staff.\n\n4. Functional Descriptions\n   - Trainer Management: Record detailed trainer profiles, including employee numbers, personal information, and employment dates. Track qualifications and course assignments.\n   - Course Management: Maintain a catalog of courses with unique identifiers, durations, fees, prerequisites, and associated hardware/software requirements.\n   - Class Scheduling: Schedule classes with details on course, trainer, classroom, and dates. Assign unique reference numbers for identification.\n   - Client Management: Store client profiles with unique client numbers, contact details, and enrollment histories. Manage membership types and discounts.\n   - Enrollment Processing: Handle client enrollment requests, confirm attendance, manage waitlists, and process payments.\n   - Hardware & Software Tracking: Monitor hardware and software used in courses, including operating systems and license numbers.\n   - Book Orders: Manage course books, track ISBNs, authors, prices, and vendor orders. Record order status, deliveries, and shipment details.\n\n5. Non-Functional Descriptions\n   - Scalability: Support future expansion of courses, trainers, and clients.\n   - Security: Ensure data confidentiality and secure access to sensitive information.\n   - Reliability: Maintain high availability and integrity of the database system.\n   - Usability: Design user-friendly interfaces for easy navigation and data entry.\n   - Performance: Optimize system performance to handle multiple operations and users efficiently.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_codellama13b/0225.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0225\nCREATE TABLE `employees` (\n  `employee_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `contact_info` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `employment_history` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `qualifications` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`employee_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `clients` (\n  `client_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `contact_info` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `enrollment_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`client_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `courses` (\n  `course_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `course_length` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `fee` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `level` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`course_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `course_materials` (\n  `material_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `book_title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `publisher` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `list_price` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`material_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `authors` (\n  `author_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `bio` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`author_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `course_prerequisites` (\n  `prerequisite_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `course_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `prerequisite_course_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`prerequisite_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `course_prerequisites_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`course_id`) REFERENCES `courses` (`course_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `course_prerequisites_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`prerequisite_course_id`) REFERENCES `courses` (`course_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `course_software` (\n  `software_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `course_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `software_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`software_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `course_software_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`course_id`) REFERENCES `courses` (`course_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `classes` (\n  `class_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `start_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `end_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `trainer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `classroom` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `course_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`class_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `classes_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`trainer_id`) REFERENCES `employees` (`employee_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `classes_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`course_id`) REFERENCES `courses` (`course_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `enrollment_requests` (\n  `request_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `request_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `payment` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `client_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`request_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `enrollment_requests_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`client_id`) REFERENCES `clients` (`client_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `vendors` (\n  `vendor_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `contact_info` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`vendor_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `orders` (\n  `order_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `order_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `order_status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `vendor_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`order_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `orders_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`vendor_id`) REFERENCES `vendors` (`vendor_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `shipments` (\n  `shipment_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `shipment_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `vendor_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`shipment_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `shipments_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`vendor_id`) REFERENCES `vendors` (`vendor_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `order_lines` (\n  `order_line_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `order_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `material_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `quantity_ordered` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `price_charged` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`order_line_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `order_lines_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`order_id`) REFERENCES `orders` (`order_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `order_lines_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`material_id`) REFERENCES `course_materials` (`material_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `shipment_lines` (\n  `shipment_line_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `shipment_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `material_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `quantity_received` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`shipment_line_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `shipment_lines_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`shipment_id`) REFERENCES `shipments` (`shipment_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `shipment_lines_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`material_id`) REFERENCES `course_materials` (`material_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `course_book_vendors` (\n  `course_book_vendor_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `material_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `vendor_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`course_book_vendor_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `course_book_vendors_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`material_id`) REFERENCES `course_materials` (`material_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `course_book_vendors_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`vendor_id`) REFERENCES `vendors` (`vendor_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
